00:25:10,820 --> 00:25:13,300
 But Isaiah 49, 15, as one reference would say,

587
00:25:13,300 --> 00:25:14,900
 "Can a woman forget her nursing child,

588
00:25:14,900 --> 00:25:17,940
 "that she should have no compassion on the son of her womb?

589
00:25:17,940 --> 00:25:22,460
 "Even these may forget, yet I will not forget you."

590
00:25:22,460 --> 00:25:24,540
 Others of you think God doesn't have good

591
00:25:24,540 --> 00:25:25,700
 in store for my future.

592
00:25:25,700 --> 00:25:26,640
 Romans 8, 28 would say,

593
00:25:26,640 --> 00:25:28,800
 "And we know that for those who love God,

594
00:25:28,800 --> 00:25:31,640
 "all things work together for good,

595
00:25:31,640 --> 00:25:33,980
 "for those who called according to his purposes."

596
00:25:33,980 --> 00:25:34,820
 You see, friends,

597
00:25:34,820 --> 00:25:37,180
 God isn't asking you to forget your problems,

598
00:25:37,180 --> 00:25:39,700
 but he is certainly asking you to remember his promises.

599
00:25:39,700 --> 00:25:40,540
 So are you?

600
00:25:40,540 --> 00:25:49,720
 Or are you just remembering your frustrations?

601
00:25:49,720 --> 00:25:54,900
 Are you just remembering your pains?

602
00:25:54,900 --> 00:25:58,560
 Are you just remembering your hardships?

603
00:25:58,560 --> 00:26:00,600
 Again, this text teaches us very clearly,

604
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:02,300
 he does not belittle those things,

605
00:26:04,180 --> 00:26:06,300
 but he does oversee those things.

606
00:26:06,300 --> 00:26:09,500
 And his word has something to say about it.

607
00:26:09,500 --> 00:26:10,900
 That's why, listen to me,

608
00:26:10,900 --> 00:26:11,900
 if you don't have one of these,

609
00:26:11,900 --> 00:26:13,000
 we would love to give you one.

610
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:14,500
 You can walk out to the welcome desk

611
00:26:14,500 --> 00:26:17,180
 and our team would love to give you a copy of the scripture

612
00:26:17,180 --> 00:26:20,100
 because you need to know what this says.

613
00:26:20,100 --> 00:26:21,820
 It's easy to know what you think.

614
00:26:21,820 --> 00:26:25,060
 It's another thing entirely to know what he says.

615
00:26:25,060 --> 00:26:28,180
 This book, this book is not just a Christian reference book.

616
00:26:28,180 --> 00:26:31,420
 Like this thing, this thing is not a theological dictionary

617
00:26:31,420 --> 00:26:32,660
 that just helps you to understand

618
00:26:32,660 --> 00:26:34,860
 concept theological ideals.

619
00:26:34,860 --> 00:26:38,440
 This book, this book is not a moral handbook

620
00:26:38,440 --> 00:26:39,980
 that's teaching you the rules of the game

621
00:26:39,980 --> 00:26:42,020
 so you don't get in trouble with God.

622
00:26:42,020 --> 00:26:46,020
 This book is not a moral grab bag or a devotional grab bag.

623
00:26:46,020 --> 00:26:47,580
 Like it's not just something that you go to

624
00:26:47,580 --> 00:26:49,820
 to kind of flip through, point a finger down

625
00:26:49,820 --> 00:26:51,700
 and take something inspirational to encourage you

626
00:26:51,700 --> 00:26:53,260
 and move you forward in your day.

627
00:26:53,260 --> 00:26:54,740
 That's not what this is.

628
00:26:54,740 --> 00:26:59,220
 This is the written, spoken revelation of God.

629
00:26:59,220 --> 00:27:03,700
 It is a story about the character and nature of him

630
00:27:03,700 --> 00:27:05,700
 as revealed through his son.

631
00:27:05,700 --> 00:27:07,200
 And he has given it to you

632
00:27:07,200 --> 00:27:10,300
 because he wants you to know him personally.

633
00:27:10,300 --> 00:27:11,900
 He's not signing you up for anything

634
00:27:11,900 --> 00:27:13,620
 other than relationship.

635
00:27:13,620 --> 00:27:16,580
 He has something that he wants to speak to your life

636
00:27:16,580 --> 00:27:21,420
 in the face of your worry and waiting.

637
00:27:21,420 --> 00:27:25,760
 So will you open it and let him speak?

638
00:27:25,760 --> 00:27:29,020
 It's easy to remember your pain.

639
00:27:29,020 --> 00:27:31,540
 It's another thing to remember his promises.

640
00:27:31,540 --> 00:27:34,020
 That's what Jeremiah does.

641
00:27:34,020 --> 00:27:37,220
 As we keep going, we see he knows who God is

642
00:27:37,220 --> 00:27:39,520
 and he preaches who God is to himself.

643
00:27:39,520 --> 00:27:41,420
 He says this in verse 22.

644
00:27:41,420 --> 00:27:45,860
 He says, "The steadfast love of the Lord never ceases.

645
00:27:45,860 --> 00:27:48,280
 "His mercies, they never come to an end.

646
00:27:48,280 --> 00:27:49,840
 "They're new every morning.

647
00:27:49,840 --> 00:27:51,260
 "Great is your faithfulness.

648
00:27:51,260 --> 00:27:53,800
 "The Lord is my portion, says my soul.

649
00:27:53,800 --> 00:27:56,380
 "Therefore I will hope in him."

650
00:27:57,860 --> 00:28:00,540
 Famous verses, some of you remember them

651
00:28:00,540 --> 00:28:02,700
 because you've sung them in the times past.

652
00:28:02,700 --> 00:28:05,900
 What's fascinating about these verses

653
00:28:05,900 --> 00:28:10,500
 is they are dead center

654
00:28:10,500 --> 00:28:17,440
 of the saddest book in the entire Bible.

655
00:28:17,440 --> 00:28:21,860
 And they are some of the most hope-filled verses

656
00:28:21,860 --> 00:28:24,120
 found in the entire scripture.

657
00:28:24,120 --> 00:28:26,180
 If you're tracking theological theming

658
00:28:26,180 --> 00:28:27,460
 through the book of Lamentations,

659
00:28:27,460 --> 00:28:29,020
 this is the center of it all.

660
00:28:29,020 --> 00:28:33,180
 This is the idea that God is trying to draw you towards.

661
00:28:33,180 --> 00:28:34,780
 You think that's coincidental?

662
00:28:34,780 --> 00:28:37,020
 No.

663
00:28:37,020 --> 00:28:41,180
 Like he's trying to tell you the second thing

664
00:28:41,180 --> 00:28:42,900
 that will give you the secret to waiting well,

665
00:28:42,900 --> 00:28:47,100
 that your delay is an invitation to come deeper with God.

666
00:28:47,100 --> 00:28:50,580
 Your delay is an invitation to go deeper with God.

667
00:28:50,580 --> 00:28:54,980
 Like the Hebrew here for God's love, it's the word hesed.

668
00:28:54,980 --> 00:28:56,660
 Hesed's a really difficult word

669
00:28:56,660 --> 00:28:58,220
 to actually translate into English

670
00:28:58,220 --> 00:29:01,860
 because it comprises more than just love as a feeling.

671
00:29:01,860 --> 00:29:03,900
 It describes love as an action.

672
00:29:03,900 --> 00:29:05,300
 So just to help give you an idea

673
00:29:05,300 --> 00:29:08,900
 of what actual hesed, steadfast love looks like.

674
00:29:08,900 --> 00:29:10,780
 I remember there was a gentleman that I knew from church

675
00:29:10,780 --> 00:29:13,520
 when I lived in Houston and his wife had dementia.

676
00:29:13,520 --> 00:29:19,780
 And what that meant is she struggled to remember who he was.

677
00:29:19,780 --> 00:29:25,520
 She could not recall the memories they'd once made.

678
00:29:25,520 --> 00:29:29,740
 She couldn't retell the stories that they shared.

679
00:29:29,740 --> 00:29:33,620
 She was growing to become a stranger to him.

680
00:29:33,620 --> 00:29:37,080
 And yet, despite the fact that this was true,

681
00:29:37,080 --> 00:29:44,020
 every day he would show up and speak to her.

682
00:29:44,020 --> 00:29:45,900
 He would show up and he would feed her.

683
00:29:45,900 --> 00:29:48,060
 He would show up and he would advocate for her.

684
00:29:48,060 --> 00:29:50,460
 He would show up and he would love her

685
00:29:50,460 --> 00:29:55,460
 because he was bound not just by the feeling of love,

686
00:29:56,400 --> 00:29:58,640
 but the choice of love.

687
00:29:58,640 --> 00:30:02,720
 A love that is loyal, that is unfailing,

688
00:30:02,720 --> 00:30:07,720
 that is unending, undying, a love the likes of which God

689
00:30:07,720 --> 00:30:10,200
 is most specifically characterized by.

690
00:30:10,200 --> 00:30:13,560
 This is the kind of God that loves you in your waiting.

691
00:30:13,560 --> 00:30:17,600
 250 times in the scripture, it speaks of this love

692
00:30:17,600 --> 00:30:19,720
 because it wants us to know

693
00:30:19,720 --> 00:30:22,480
 that God is full of this kind of love.

694
00:30:24,240 --> 00:30:27,120
 So if God loves us this kind of way,

695
00:30:27,120 --> 00:30:32,280
 why the heck does he lead us into seasons of waiting?

696
00:30:32,280 --> 00:30:34,320
 That feels pretty unloving, right?

697
00:30:34,320 --> 00:30:35,720
 Like, hey, I've got a great dream for you,

698
00:30:35,720 --> 00:30:37,320
 but you're gonna sit over here and you're gonna have

699
00:30:37,320 --> 00:30:40,320
 to endure for a very long time until it arrives.

700
00:30:40,320 --> 00:30:41,280
 Why would he do that?

701
00:30:41,280 --> 00:30:42,960
 Like, God, that's not loving in the slightest.

702
00:30:42,960 --> 00:30:45,300
 Like, come on, man, you say you love me,

703
00:30:45,300 --> 00:30:47,240
 but this feels so unloving.

704
00:30:47,240 --> 00:30:49,640
 And it feels even more unloving when we consider

705
00:30:49,640 --> 00:30:53,360
 the things that we actually want as good.

706
00:30:53,360 --> 00:30:56,960
 Like, it's not like God's just against the things

707
00:30:56,960 --> 00:30:57,840
 you want that are bad.

708
00:30:57,840 --> 00:30:59,540
 Sometimes it feels like God is against the things

709
00:30:59,540 --> 00:31:00,680
 you want that are good.

710
00:31:00,680 --> 00:31:05,680
 So in here, who wants to be happy in their job?

711
00:31:05,680 --> 00:31:09,720
 Show of hands, anybody wanna be happy in their job?

712
00:31:09,720 --> 00:31:10,560
 Is God against that?

713
00:31:10,560 --> 00:31:15,200
 No, like we know God, he was the one that created work

714
00:31:15,200 --> 00:31:19,960
 and he meant for you to do it unto your fulfillment in him.

715
00:31:19,960 --> 00:31:21,880
 Anybody here wanna find a spouse?

716
00:31:21,880 --> 00:31:23,280
 You just throw up your hand.

717
00:31:23,280 --> 00:31:24,520
 It's not like we don't know you didn't come here

718
00:31:24,520 --> 00:31:26,120
 for this already.

719
00:31:26,120 --> 00:31:27,400
 Yeah, man.

720
00:31:27,400 --> 00:31:28,880
 It's funny, some of you put your hands down,

721
00:31:28,880 --> 00:31:30,480
 others got your hand up 'cause you're still hoping

722
00:31:30,480 --> 00:31:32,600
 somebody will take notice.

723
00:31:32,600 --> 00:31:35,720
 Scripture tells us, he who finds a wife finds a good thing.

724
00:31:35,720 --> 00:31:37,320
 God's not against that good desire.

725
00:31:37,320 --> 00:31:41,380
 Anybody in here need healing, experiencing pain,

726
00:31:41,380 --> 00:31:44,280
 or wanting healing for someone else.

727
00:31:44,280 --> 00:31:46,080
 God's not against that.

728
00:31:46,080 --> 00:31:50,920
 Revelation 21 tells us that he's going to wipe away

729
00:31:50,920 --> 00:31:53,840
 every tear, he's gonna right every wrong,

730
00:31:53,840 --> 00:31:55,320
 he's gonna heal all pain.

731
00:31:55,320 --> 00:31:58,280
 Jesus did not come for the healthy, he came for the sick.

732
00:31:58,280 --> 00:32:00,480
 Anybody in here want clarity about something?

733
00:32:00,480 --> 00:32:04,120
 God's not a God of confusion, not a God of chaos,

734
00:32:04,120 --> 00:32:05,960
 a God of peace and order.

735
00:32:05,960 --> 00:32:07,280
 Anybody want joy?

736
00:32:07,280 --> 00:32:11,340
 You don't put your hand up on this one, you're crazy.

737
00:32:11,340 --> 00:32:13,360
 Because this is what the world wants.

738
00:32:13,360 --> 00:32:15,500
 The world wants to be happy, happiness and joy.

739
00:32:15,500 --> 00:32:17,880
 They are not disconnected ideas in the scripture.

740
00:32:17,880 --> 00:32:19,480
 It's the same word throughout the Bible

741
00:32:19,480 --> 00:32:21,360
 for both of these concepts.

742
00:32:21,360 --> 00:32:24,120
 And what we know is that Jesus in his presence

743
00:32:24,120 --> 00:32:25,120
 is fullness of joy.

744
00:32:25,120 --> 00:32:27,840
 He came to give you life and life abundantly.

745
00:32:27,840 --> 00:32:30,240
 Anybody in here looking for community?

746
00:32:30,240 --> 00:32:31,560
 If so, you're in the right place.

747
00:32:31,560 --> 00:32:32,400
 Welcome to the church.

748
00:32:32,400 --> 00:32:34,920
 We would love to show you that Christ didn't just save you

749
00:32:34,920 --> 00:32:37,480
 from your sin, he saved you into his people.

750
00:32:37,480 --> 00:32:39,480
 We would love to get connected with you.

751
00:32:39,480 --> 00:32:42,120
 These are good things,

752
00:32:42,120 --> 00:32:44,940
 things that we have all attested to wanting.

753
00:32:44,940 --> 00:32:47,520
 Why then is God making us wait for them?

754
00:32:48,520 --> 00:32:50,800
 This is important.

755
00:32:50,800 --> 00:32:54,800
 Because he knows the depth of your wanting

756
00:32:54,800 --> 00:32:58,120
 is revealed by the length of your waiting.

757
00:32:58,120 --> 00:33:00,880
 So what I mean by that is this.

758
00:33:00,880 --> 00:33:03,720
 If you came to me and you said you were hungry

759
00:33:03,720 --> 00:33:04,800
 and I said, hey man,

760
00:33:04,800 --> 00:33:08,060
 I'll go buy you a steak at Applebee's right now.

761
00:33:08,060 --> 00:33:14,040
 Or I'll buy you a steak at Bob's in six hours.

762
00:33:14,860 --> 00:33:17,600
 Chances are you're waiting for Bob's.

763
00:33:17,600 --> 00:33:18,600
 Why?

764
00:33:18,600 --> 00:33:22,360
 Because the depth of your wanting for Bob's

765
00:33:22,360 --> 00:33:24,540
 is revealed by the length of your waiting,

766
00:33:24,540 --> 00:33:26,400
 the willingness to hold off

767
00:33:26,400 --> 00:33:28,520
 and get what you ultimately want.

768
00:33:28,520 --> 00:33:33,100
 You see, we will wait longest for what we want most.

769
00:33:33,100 --> 00:33:36,840
 And yet your impatience towards God

770
00:33:36,840 --> 00:33:38,800
 reveals your idolatry against him.

771
00:33:38,800 --> 00:33:42,140
 (congregation laughing)

772
00:33:42,140 --> 00:33:45,740
 All throughout the Bible,

773
00:33:45,740 --> 00:33:47,940
 we see people forcing God's timing

774
00:33:47,940 --> 00:33:49,140
 instead of following it

775
00:33:49,140 --> 00:33:51,860
 because they want the gift more than the giver

776
00:33:51,860 --> 00:33:53,460
 and it never goes well for them.

777
00:33:53,460 --> 00:33:56,540
 It always ends in disaster.

778
00:33:56,540 --> 00:34:01,900
 Abraham was unwilling to wait for God

779
00:34:01,900 --> 00:34:03,420
 to make good on his promise.

780
00:34:03,420 --> 00:34:06,180
 And so he had Ishmael.

781
00:34:07,320 --> 00:34:10,080
 Jacob was unwilling to wait on the blessings

782
00:34:10,080 --> 00:34:12,280
 that God promised to him

783
00:34:12,280 --> 00:34:14,360
 and so he stole it from his father.

784
00:34:14,360 --> 00:34:16,120
 Moses was unwilling to wait for God

785
00:34:16,120 --> 00:34:17,400
 to deliver the nation of Israel

786
00:34:17,400 --> 00:34:20,160
 so he murdered a man and he buried him in the sand.

787
00:34:20,160 --> 00:34:22,600
 Israel as a country was unwilling to wait

788
00:34:22,600 --> 00:34:24,640
 for Moses to come down from the mountain

789
00:34:24,640 --> 00:34:26,280
 and so they made the golden calf.

790
00:34:26,280 --> 00:34:28,000
 Saul was unwilling to wait for Samuel

791
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:31,120
 to offer sacrifices before going into battle

792
00:34:31,120 --> 00:34:32,840
 and because he wasn't willing to wait,

793
00:34:32,840 --> 00:34:35,160
 the kingdom was torn from him.

794
00:34:35,160 --> 00:34:37,300
 I can go on but the point is very simple.

